02:31:56,580 --> 02:31:59,860
Sie konnten nicht nur eine Firmware-Update anbieten, um das Problem zu lösen.

2596
02:31:59,860 --> 02:32:08,100
Because Bitcoin has no way to rotate a key, the only way out is for victims to generate a brand new seed and move their coins with an actual on-chain transaction.

2597
02:32:08,440 --> 02:32:14,640
But of course, because this is Bitcoin, every transaction waits in the public mempool until a miner includes it in a block,

2598
02:32:14,800 --> 02:32:19,100
which means the attacker can just watch the mempool for anything coming from a compromised address.

2599
02:32:19,420 --> 02:32:26,200
They can then sign their own competing transaction with the same keys and a higher fee, and miners will confirm the highest bidder first.

2600
02:32:26,200 --> 02:32:37,960
So when a fourth attack went live on Monday morning, the only way to win was to skip the public mempool entirely and send your rescue transaction directly to a mining pool, since the bot can't outbid a transaction it never sees.

2601
02:32:38,100 --> 02:32:45,600
